  "articleBody": "It's easy to make a few common blunders when arranging your bedroom that can leave it feeling cramped and unusable. One frequent mistake is completely forgetting about the swing space for your doors and closets. You need enough room for them to open fully without hitting furniture or blocking a pathway. Another big one is not leaving enough space to actually make your bed! Trying to squeeze between a wall and your bed is a daily struggle nobody needs. Also, watch out for blocking dresser drawers or the main path at the foot of your bed. You need at least 24-36 inches of clear space there for easy movement. Many folks also just plunk furniture down without considering their main circulation path, making the room feel like an obstacle course. Before you start moving heavy items, take a minute to visualize your movement through the room. If you find yourself in a really tight spot, especially in a small room or one with multiple doors, a professional space planner can be a lifesaver. They can help you figure out the best layout to maximize both safety and comfort.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
